  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manek Nabi Kaasambhai vs State Of Gujarat on 4 March, 2024 Author: Ilesh J. Vora Bench: Ilesh J. Vora R/Cr.Ma/23159/2022 Order DATED: 04/03/2024 IN THE HIGH COURT OF GUJARAT AT AHMEDABAD R/CRIMINAL MISC.APPLICATION (FOR QUASHING & [LEAKAGE_MASK] FIR/ORDER) NO. 23159 of 2022 ========================================================== MANEK NABI KAASAMBHAI Versus STATE OF GUJARAT & ANR. ========================================================== Appearance: MR VICKY B MEHTA(5422) for the Applicant(s) No. 1 for the Respondent(s) No. 2 MR JAY MEHTA, APP for the Respondent(s) No. 1 ========================================================== CORAM:HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE ILESH J. VORA Date : 04/03/2024 ORAL ORDER 1.",
    "facts": "By invoking inherent jurisdiction of this Court under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure Code, the applicant Manik Kasambhai, has preferred this application thereby he is seeking quashment of the FIR being CR. No.11211015220301 of 2022 registered with Dhrangadhra City Police Station District Surendranagar for the offences punishable under Section 332, 337, 186, 160, 143, 147, 148, 149, 506(2), 504 and 427 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 3 of the Prevention of Damage to Public Property Act and Section 135 of the Gujarat Police Act.",
    "arguments": "6. On the other hand, learned APP Mr. Mehta, has submitted that the contentions as raised being a disputed question of fact cannot be examined at this stage as the investigation is still not completed and therefore, at this stage, powers should not exercise to thwart investigation and proceedings ought not to be scuttled at the initial stage."
  },
